- So: binary search on d, then check via greedy on perimeter order, trying each starting point

For the check: map each point to a 1D perimeter parameter, sort. Try each as starting point, greedily pick next point with perimeter distance ≥ d. After k-1 hops, verify the closing wrap-around distance is also ≥ d.

